{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You will suck the milk of nations.</b> The meaning: wealth that they will give as tribute." "<b>And the devastation of kings.</b> From the root of שדים, for the patterns of noun forms vary. (Isaiah 32:12)"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {1 "He explains שוד as derived from the same root as שדים (breasts), in keeping with the suckling imagery of the previous clause; his point is that noun patterns (משקלים) can shift within a root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:30.255509446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}